		(uuid "096bd083-ed22-467d-a594-25b1d6385134")
	)
	(text "From LED datasheet the Typical Voltage drop at 5 mA is 2.95V.\nKnowing this, I can compute the series resistor:\n	R = (3.3V - V_forw_LED) / 5 mA = 70 Ohm\n	--> E12 series (5% Toll.), R = 82 Ohm\n\nIf the Actual Forward Voltage of the LED is higher, it will simply light up with\nlower luminosity, so using the typical Forward Voltage value is ok (I don't need to \nbe precise on the actual current flowing in the LED, I just need it to light up)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 56.642 67.056 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0da14fe0-e786-4a7a-90c3-23363d84f856")
	)
	(text "Spare"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 366.522 140.716 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "106096dc-2336-4b50-b52d-3c12eea42bc8")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(thickness 0.2223)
			)
		)
		(uuid "12c223b6-a118-4d90-a99c-6de4d590ea84")
	)
	(text "Pull-Up is useful in normal operating conditions, because the\ncomparator output has Open-Drain output. The Pull-Down is used\nto set the ouput LOW when Power Supply 3V3 Analog is lost, so\nthat this Diagnostic pin returns a Fault indication to the reader (FPGA)\n\nPull-Down is 10 greater than Pull Up, so during normal operations,\nthe voltage for HIGH level is:\n	V_HIGH = 3.3V * 10R / (11R) = 3V\nThis voltage is more than enough (> V_IH = 1.7V) to be read as HIGH by the FPGA\n\nStatic consumption when output is LOW (condition with max consumption) is:\n	P_loss = (3.3^2) / 33k = 0.33 mW"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.014 223.012 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2fe7876a-f573-4e97-9def-b223da0ef3b8")
	)
	(text "Connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 336.042 127.762 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "34994a3a-fc66-4d7d-a67a-cfb20cfc687d")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", \nwhich just disconnects the \nADC Serial DataOut pin to\nthe reader. HiZ and GND \nfaults can be simulated with\nthis connector "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 295.148 46.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3932f2db-6cc0-427e-b046-b75693cb78fa")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.416 231.648 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(thickness 0.2223)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3ac3dc2d-35f6-4cc3-aa5c-b6c771a2e7bf")
	)
	(text "nCS of ADC is pull-up to 3V3_Digtal, because the nCS is shared \nbetween the channles, and so it should not depend on the correct\nfunctionality of any of the two Channel dedicated power supplies"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.076 130.556 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4863259c-9d8d-49a8-8d84-c6d0ad381e13")
	)
